      "1": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "HOLD\n\nHold let's you sample an event by arming it. After that you can send it out by releasing it. Hold is like a recording device for events.\n\n- Patch Explained -\n• In this patch the Hold node is used to adjust the attack time of the Attack Release node without disturbing the animation in process.\n• The Float value is send to both the input and the arm inlets making sure that any change made to the float is stored in the hold node.\n• Releasing the value to the Attack Release can be done manually by pressing the Trigger node.\n\n"
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 209,
          "width": 1009,
          "x": 108.203125,
          "y": 97.9921875
        },
        "class": {
